# "Target opponent": Bot1 cannot aim Outrageous Robbery at itself (refusal), while the cast at Bot2 (the control) is offered
# and exiles Bot2's top card, a Plains, with X = 1. Only the caster gets to play it: on turn 4 Bot2, the card's owner,
# is refused the Plains from exile (CR 406.3: face down, and no permission is held by Bot2) while the Island from its hand,
# the control, can be played.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Outrageous Robbery
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x8
Plains
Island x11

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#3.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Outrageous Robbery.Cast(Bot1; X: 1)
Bot1.Hand.Outrageous Robbery.Cast(Bot2; X: 1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Exile.FaceDown = Plains
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
! Bot2.Exile.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Island
Exile.Count = 1
Exile.FaceDown = Plains
